  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Social Contract</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Kosovo):  The Social Contract Activity will continue to enhance citizen engagement in government decision-making and budgetary processes at the municipal level, resulting in more effectively leveraging increasing amounts of Government of Kosovo resources toward citizen-prioritized development goals. The Activity will provide technical assistance to 15 municipalities to better align government services with citizens&apos; needs and promote citizen-driven solutions, including participatory budgeting. Efforts in the 15 municipalities will be guided by the findings of an ongoing municipal needs assessment. The Activity will continue to expand the use of innovative USAID-supported practices country-wide through changes to the legal and regulatory framework. Training, technical assistance, and support in implementing citizen-identified projects will be provided to facilitate public participation processes that are both valuable and feasible for the community and local administrations. This initiative aligns with FY24 funding priorities, supporting CAATSA Goal 2 promoting rule of law (10% of funding), supporting CAATSA Goal 4 strengthening political processes (25% of funding) and contributing to ICS Objective 2.2 by integrating public participation and budgeting processes into municipal action plans to ensure citizens&apos; needs are addressed.... .</narrative>
  </description>
